fix(dsc): give the shared-region pager the slide-info blob size

kebab_dsc_read_mappings() recorded where each mapping's dyld slide-info
blob lives (sms_slide_start) but never recorded how large it is
(sms_slide_size).  kebab_dsc_apply_slide() uses sms_slide_size to decide
whether a mapping carries slide info, so in a non-zero slide run it left
VM_PROT_SLIDE clear on all four data mappings.  vm_shared_region_map_file()
then installed plain file mappings, sr_slide still held the requested
slide, and no lazy rebase pager was created: dyld would see a slid base
whose pointer chains had never been rebased.

Set sms_slide_size from the same mapping-and-slide entry as the start
address.  The kernel still copyin()s the cache's own v2 blob in
vm_shared_region_slide() and builds nothing new; this only makes the plan
describe the blob that scripts/verify-shared-cache-plan.py validates
(0xa788/0xbc08 in .27.dylddata, 0x5350/0x6f58 in .41.dylddata).

The one-line assignment compiles in the KEBAB arm64 tree; no hardware.
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c b/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
index 2e3c51b..f0f1a82 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kebab_dyldcache.c
@@ -966,6 +966,14 @@
 		file->mappings[i].sms_slide_start =
 		    file->mappings[found].sms_address +
 		    (offset - file->mappings[found].sms_file_offset);
+		/*
+		 * vm_shared_region_slide() treats a non-zero start with a
+		 * zero size as nothing to do, and kebab_dsc_apply_slide()
+		 * uses sms_slide_size to decide whether to set VM_PROT_SLIDE.
+		 * Set both fields from the same mapping-and-slide entry, or
+		 * the slide path silently degrades to a plain mapping.
+		 */
+		file->mappings[i].sms_slide_size = size;
 		error = kebab_dsc_validate_slide_info(vp, name, i, offset, size,
 		    file->mappings[i].sms_size);
 		if (error != 0) {
